<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Soy slips, corn and wheat steady.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Soy slips, corn and wheat steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf soybean basis slipped one cent a bushel on Thursday while corn and wheat values steadied, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers noted very little farm sales in both soybeans and corn. &quot;Farmers are not selling,&quot; one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>On the export front, Pakistan was tendering on June 25 for 500,000 tonnes of optional origin white wheat, July 11-August 10 shipment, a spokesman at the country's U.S. embassy in Washington said. He said the wheat would be either from the United States, Australia or Canada.  </p>
